g Engineering Summer Programs Sample Engineering Courses Engineering News English English Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample English Courses English Program Awards English News History History Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample History Courses History News Leadership Psychology Careers in Psychology Psychology 1100 Psychology Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Student Research Psychology News Social Work Social Work Career Planning Sociology/Criminology Academic Recognition Awards Academic Support Services Campus Resource Guide Cancelled Classes Carmen Class & Exam Schedules Course Guide Honors & Undergrad Research Griffin Society Honors & Scholars Program Maintaining Honors Status Taking the Right Courses Senior Thesis Library Study Abroad Summer Semester Research Community of Scholars Faculty Accomplishments Undergraduate Research Undergrad Research Colloquium Give Giving Changes Lives Impact Report Marion Campus Funds Search Submit search Toggle search dialog Home Current Students Career Services Current Students Student Opportunity Development Fund Bookstore Buckeyes First Student Success Programming Counseling & Wellness Services STEP Program First Year Experience Dining Services Housing Student Life Student Leadership Opportunities Student Organizations Housing Homecoming Dining Services Campus Safety Campus Recreation On-Campus Student Job Opportunities Health Insurance Financial Aid Career Services Academic Support Services Career Services How will you make the most of your undergraduate career? What can you be doing to prepare yourself for success after you graduate? Whatever your path may be, whether it’s directly to a career or on to graduate or professional school you will need to begin preparing yourself for that next step. That preparation needs to begin from the moment you step foot on campus and continue throughout your time here. The Office of Career Services is here to assist you on your path to success. The office is in Maynard Hall Room 124. The office can assist students with career planning, major exploration, job and internship searches, graduate school preparation, resumes, cover letters and interview preparation. For more information or to schedule an appointment, contact the office at 740-725-6334 or email Jane Arnold – Coordinator of Career Services at MarionCareers@osu.edu Please use the links for additional resources and information. View career-related events on Handshake Employer Registration Marion Campus Job Fair The Ohio State University Home The Ohio State University at Marion 1465 Mount Vernon Avenue Marion, OH 43302 askmarion@osu.edu Phone: 740-389-6786 Facebook\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external Instagram\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external X\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external LinkedIn\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external YouTube\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external If you have a disability and experience difficulty accessing this content, please contact us . Privacy Statement Non-discrimination Notice Cookie Settings Site Map © 2026 The Ohio State University Back to top"
