    "https://osumarion.osu.edu/current-students/student-jobs": {
      "title": "On-Campus Job Opportunities",
      "description": "On-Campus Job Opportunities | The Ohio State University at Marion Skip to main content Show Links OSU.edu Buckeye Link Map Webmail Search Ohio State Future Students Admissions Contact Us Financial Aid Housing Majors and Programs Regional Campus Commitment Program Orientation Meet the Support Services Team Parent and Family Resources Resources for Admitted Buckeyes Visit Current Students Academic Support Services Bookstore Buckeyes First Career Services Counseling & Wellness Services Dining Services Financial Aid First Year Experience Health Insurance Housing On-Campus Student Job Opportunities STEP Program Student Life Campus Recreation Discount and Giveaway Donation Form FAQ Policies Student ID Campus Safety Dining Services Homecoming Housing Student Leadership Opportunities Student Organizations Student Opportunity Development Fund Student Success Programming Information for Students Alumni Alumni Hall of Fame Buckeye Backers Delaware Alumni Club Marion Alumni Club Ohio State Alumni Association Transcripts Outreach About Us Dean’s Student Advisory Board External Event Reservations Ohio State Marion Board Community Outreach AI for the Community Buckeye Talks on Tap Build Your Own Prairie The Downtown Engagement Hub Larry R. Yoder Prairie Learning Laboratory Pelotonia Team Marion Ralph W. Howard Service Award Warren G. Harding Symposium Cultural Arts Five Nights on Campus Kuhn Fine Art Gallery The Art of the Pair Educational Partnerships GoBuck$ Pay It Forward Pride & Life Skills Mentoring Program 60 Robotics Competition Teacher Manufacturing Boot Camp Youth Programs Academics Academic Calendar Academic Majors & Programs Associate of Arts Degree Biology Biology Majors & Minors Center for Life Sciences Education Major Requirements Resources & Opportunities Summer Programs Biology News Education College Credit Plus Teaching and Learning Pathways Field Experiences & Resources Education News Engineering Technology Engineering Career Opportunities in Engineering Engineering Summer Programs Sample Engineering Courses Engineering News English English Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample English Courses English Program Awards English News History History Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample History Courses History News Leadership Psychology Careers in Psychology Psychology 1100 Psychology Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Student Research Psychology News Social Work Social Work Career Planning Sociology/Criminology Academic Recognition Awards Academic Support Services Campus Resource Guide Cancelled Classes Carmen Class & Exam Schedules Course Guide Honors & Undergrad Research Griffin Society Honors & Scholars Program Maintaining Honors Status Taking the Right Courses Senior Thesis Library Study Abroad Summer Semester Research Community of Scholars Faculty Accomplishments Undergraduate Research Undergrad Research Colloquium Give Giving Changes Lives Impact Report Marion Campus Funds Search Submit search Toggle search dialog Home Current Students On-Campus Job Opportunities On-Campus Job Opportunities The Ohio State University at Marion hires many new student workers across departments each semester. If you are interested in student employment at Ohio State Marion, please review the job listings below. Job listing updates come from the hiring department. If a posting needs updated please email peregrina.3@osu.edu or rowe.31@osu.edu or contact the hiring department. Below may not be a complete listing of on-campus student jobs. If the position is missing a link to apply, the position is currently not hiring and/or filled. View full list of student jobs Advising Office Student Assistant (R106526) The Advising office is currently hiring students to assist students, visitors, answer phones, direct calls, monitor campus switchboard, take messages, and make appointments for advisors. What we are looking for: Detail-oriented ability to produce neat, error-free work Proofread for grammatical and typographical errors Enjoys working with people Good organizational and verbal communication skills Knowledge of and ability to use computer and various computer programs (Word, Excel, etc.) What we offer: Employment for work study students Flexible work schedule around classes Leadership development Experience working in a team environment APPLY LINK: https://www.myworkday.com/osu/d/inst/15$158872/9925$182882.htmld FOR QUESTIONS: For any questions about the application process or job description please email Shellie Shirk at shirk.20@osu.edu Pay Rate: $13/hr Compost Champion https://www.myworkday.com/osu/d/inst/1$14180/5303$117275.htmld Job Description Ohio State Marion is seeking enthusiastic and dependable students to serve as Compost Champions, supporting the campus's growing sustainability and expanded waste management program. Compost Champions play a key role in collecting and processing food waste through the campus composting program while helping educate the campus community about sustainable practices. Under the guidance of Ohio State Marion staff, Compost Champions will assist with the basic operation of the campus composter located behind the Ohio State Marion Library and help ensure compost collection stations remain clean, functional, and accessible. This paid position offers hands-on experience in sustainability and maintenance operations. Key Responsibilities Collect compost material from designated compost collection sites across campus. Replace and re-line compost collection bins. Weigh, track, and accurately record food waste collection data. Load collected food waste into the on-site composting system. Unload finished compost from the composter and prepare it for pick-up. Maintain a clean, safe, and organized worksite. Monitor compost collection bins and report maintenance or operational concerns. Be a champion: Lead by example and educate students in supporting campus sustainability initiatives and responsible waste management. Qualifications Available to be on the Ohio State Marion campus most days each week. Currently enrolled and in good academic standing with the university. Reliable, self-motivated, and able to work independently with minimal supervision. Demonstrated interest in sustainability. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to perform light physical tasks, including lifting, carrying, and moving compost collection containers and materials. Schedule: Split workweek with another Compost Champion (typically 2–3 days per week per student) Hours: 1–2 hours per shift, primarily during evening hours Help Desk Support Student (R106397) Department: OCIO 100% of job duties listed below: 1.    Answer helpdesk phone in a professional manner and take detailed  messages for IT staff. 2.    Open and close General Computer Lab LC220 for scheduled hours. 3.    Complete classroom maintenance and cleaning weekly. 4.    Assist students in computer lab with general IT support. 5.    Assist faculty in Library Classrooms with IT needs. 6.    Load paper and toner in printers and reorder supplies as needed. 7.    Process and document surplus equipment. 8.    Assist with IT projects as needed on campus. 9. Process, tag, and inventory new equipment. 10. Deploy and collect student loaner devices. Additional Information: Our goal is to foster a community of professionals with diverse skills, experiences and backgrounds who actively collaborate to support the mission of the Ohio State University. We are committed to personal and professional growth of individuals as they achieve their highest potential and support others along the way. In an ever-changing technology landscape our employees are flexible, innovative, and adept problem-solvers. The Ohio State University Home The Ohio State University at Marion 1465 Mount Vernon Avenue Marion, OH 43302 askmarion@osu.edu Phone: 740-389-6786 Facebook\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external Instagram\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external X\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external LinkedIn\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external YouTube\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external If you have a disability and experience difficulty accessing this content, please contact us . Privacy Statement Non-discrimination Notice Cookie Settings Site Map © 2026 The Ohio State University Back to top"
