    "https://osumarion.osu.edu/academics/majors/social-work/social-work-career-planning": {
      "title": "Social Work Career Planning",
      "description": "Social Work | The Ohio State University at Marion Skip to main content Show Links OSU.edu Buckeye Link Map Webmail Search Ohio State Future Students Admissions Contact Us Financial Aid Housing Majors and Programs Regional Campus Commitment Program Orientation Meet the Support Services Team Parent and Family Resources Resources for Admitted Buckeyes Visit Current Students Academic Support Services Bookstore Buckeyes First Career Services Counseling & Wellness Services Dining Services Financial Aid First Year Experience Health Insurance Housing On-Campus Student Job Opportunities STEP Program Student Life Campus Recreation Discount and Giveaway Donation Form FAQ Policies Student ID Campus Safety Dining Services Homecoming Housing Student Leadership Opportunities Student Organizations Student Opportunity Development Fund Student Success Programming Information for Students Alumni Alumni Hall of Fame Buckeye Backers Delaware Alumni Club Marion Alumni Club Ohio State Alumni Association Transcripts Outreach About Us Dean’s Student Advisory Board External Event Reservations Ohio State Marion Board Community Outreach AI for the Community Buckeye Talks on Tap Build Your Own Prairie The Downtown Engagement Hub Larry R. Yoder Prairie Learning Laboratory Pelotonia Team Marion Ralph W. Howard Service Award Warren G. Harding Symposium Cultural Arts Five Nights on Campus Kuhn Fine Art Gallery The Art of the Pair Educational Partnerships GoBuck$ Pay It Forward Pride & Life Skills Mentoring Program 60 Robotics Competition Teacher Manufacturing Boot Camp Youth Programs Academics Academic Calendar Academic Majors & Programs Associate of Arts Degree Biology Biology Majors & Minors Center for Life Sciences Education Major Requirements Resources & Opportunities Summer Programs Biology News Education College Credit Plus Teaching and Learning Pathways Field Experiences & Resources Education News Engineering Technology Engineering Career Opportunities in Engineering Engineering Summer Programs Sample Engineering Courses Engineering News English English Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample English Courses English Program Awards English News History History Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample History Courses History News Leadership Psychology Careers in Psychology Psychology 1100 Psychology Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Student Research Psychology News Social Work Social Work Career Planning Sociology/Criminology Academic Recognition Awards Academic Support Services Campus Resource Guide Cancelled Classes Carmen Class & Exam Schedules Course Guide Honors & Undergrad Research Griffin Society Honors & Scholars Program Maintaining Honors Status Taking the Right Courses Senior Thesis Library Study Abroad Summer Semester Research Community of Scholars Faculty Accomplishments Undergraduate Research Undergrad Research Colloquium Give Giving Changes Lives Impact Report Marion Campus Funds Search Submit search Toggle search dialog Home Academics Academic Majors and Programs Social Work Social Work Career Planning Academics Honors & Undergrad Research Summer Semester Academic Support Services Academic Majors & Programs Sociology/Criminology Leadership Engineering Associate of Arts Degree Engineering Technology Social Work Social Work Career Planning Education College Credit Plus Teaching and Learning Pathways Field Experiences & Resources Education News Psychology Careers in Psychology Psychology 1100 Psychology Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Student Research Psychology News History History Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample History Courses History News English English Majors & Minors Resources & Opportunities Sample English Courses English Program Awards English News Biology Study Abroad Course Guide Library Carmen Class & Exam Schedules Cancelled Classes Campus Resource Guide Academic Calendar Academic Recognition Awards Social Work Career Planning Students who pursue a degree in social work have a broad range of career possibilities. Graduates are Licenced Social Worker (LSW) eligible and prepared to work in careers such as: aging and gerontology child and family welfare developmental disabilities domestic violence health care homelessness justice and corrections international social work mental health policy and planning (local, state and national level) school social work substance abuse treatment Social workers are administrators, therapists, community organizers, educators, and researchers. They work with a diverse population, helping people in large cities and in small communities. Some students use the undergraduate social work major as preparation for various other graduate and professional programs including business, law, medicine, and public health. What our students say about the Bachelor of Social Work and a career in Social Work Expanding Your Education: Masters of Social Work Many students use the undergraduate social work major as preparation for graduate school in social work. Students who have undergraduate degrees in social work and meet the criteria for the ASAP option can apply for accelerated master of social work (MSW) programs (ASAP: Advanced Standing Student Plan: available Columbus campus only). Those with a bachelor’s degree in social work not meeting this criteria can apply for the Regular option. An MSW degree prepares students for advanced practice and is necessary to provide mental health counseling in most states. Graduates are LISW-eligible. The Ohio State University Home The Ohio State University at Marion 1465 Mount Vernon Avenue Marion, OH 43302 askmarion@osu.edu Phone: 740-389-6786 Facebook\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external Instagram\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external X\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external LinkedIn\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external YouTube\n        \t\t\t        \t\t\t\tprofile — external If you have a disability and experience